WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Every year, in villages across Karnataka,
children walk to a school like this one.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.519
They carry everything they own in one bag.

00:00:12.519 --> 00:00:16.290
They are bright, and
they are ready to learn.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:24.140
And somewhere between that walk and
the classroom, a school fee decides.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:33.860
For ten years, one Trust has stood at
exactly that point, one child at a time.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.081
The Trust was founded by Charulatha M. R.

00:00:39.081 --> 00:00:42.856
She had been paying school
fees for neighbourhood

00:00:42.856 --> 00:00:45.860
children long before there was a Trust.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.830
She was joined by S. M.

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:55.570
Manjunatha of Sadenahalli, the first in
his family to leave the village to study.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:02.570
In 2016 they made their first
school visit. Chickaballapur.
One child. One scholarship.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.474
On the same visit, a
hundred and fifty students

00:01:11.474 --> 00:01:14.430
received steel plates and steel glasses.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:23.000
In 2017, one became ten. Ten
students received scholarships,
and the work simply continued.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:32.140
Year after year, the same roads,
the same schools, and more children.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.923
Nobody photographs the ordinary years.

00:01:37.923 --> 00:01:41.000
These are the years the work is made of.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.684
In 2020 schools closed
and families lost work.

00:01:47.684 --> 00:01:52.570
The Trust published a single
page, and the help did not stop.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.018
In 2022 the shelves went up.

00:01:57.018 --> 00:02:02.710
Libraries in rural schools, filled with
donated story books and academic books.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:10.140
And unused notebooks, because a
book nobody opens is not a library.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.748
In 2023, career guidance for
ninth and tenth standard students,

00:02:18.748 --> 00:02:22.140
at the age when a decision
quietly gets made.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.652
The same year the map
widened. Mysore. H.D. Kote.

00:02:28.652 --> 00:02:31.430
And the tribal schools beyond them.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.012
None of this happens from an office.

00:02:37.012 --> 00:02:40.945
A principal or a neighbour
puts a name forward.

00:02:40.945 --> 00:02:44.710
The team drives out and
sits with the family.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:52.600
The Trust covers up to seventy-five per
cent of the school fee. Not all of it.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.000
The family carries the rest.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.368
A scholarship on its
own is not an education.

00:02:59.368 --> 00:03:03.710
So there are bags, notebooks,
stationery and drawing kits.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:11.229
In 2024 the Trust opened the school
year at the tribal schools of M.M.

00:03:11.229 --> 00:03:15.860
Hills, with two hundred school
bags, notebooks and stationery.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.331
Loaded into a car boot in the city.

00:03:21.331 --> 00:03:23.140
Carried in by hand.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:28.062
And in 2025, in H.D. Kote, three hundred.

00:03:28.062 --> 00:03:31.430
This time with Nisarga
Foundation beside us.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.667
No stage. No handover photograph.

00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:41.000
Just a field, and a bag for every child.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:48.515
With the children at the tribal
schools, the team stays a few days.

00:03:48.515 --> 00:03:53.290
They teach, they learn, and
then the bags are handed over.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:04:00.000
There are games, drawing, reading, and a
stage on which children sing and dance.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:06.705
And the work reaches children it
would have been easier not to reach.

00:04:06.705 --> 00:04:08.545
Children of single parents.

00:04:08.545 --> 00:04:11.000
Children from HIV-affected families.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.763
The record that matters
is a list of names.

00:04:15.763 --> 00:04:20.710
Volunteers who are advocates, engineers,
counsellors, doctors and homemakers.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:29.695
Donors in Bengaluru and
Chennai, in America, Britain,
Germany, Denmark and Dubai.

00:04:29.695 --> 00:04:33.000
Teachers who picked up
a phone about one child.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:38.386
In June 2024 a Kannada daily
carried the work from Mulbagal.

00:04:38.386 --> 00:04:43.430
In December 2025 the Founder received
the Bharat Shiksha Ratan Award.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:51.275
Ten years. One promise, kept
quietly, one child at a time.

00:04:51.275 --> 00:04:56.000
Welcome to the tenth anniversary
of Law Park Educational Trust.

